    "q-128394": {
      "dom_id": "step-q128394",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$(-7)\\cdot (-3)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of two negative numbers, $-7$ and $-3.$ So the product will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-7)\\cdot (-3)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $7$ and $3$ without any signs: $7\\cdot 3=21.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-7)\\cdot (-3)=21.\n$$",
