      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$(-12)\\cdot (-3)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of two negative numbers, $-12$ and $-3.$ So the product will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-12)\\cdot (-3)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $12$ and $3$ without any signs: $12\\cdot 3=36.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-12)\\cdot (-3)=36.\n$$",
