      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$(-8)\\cdot (-6)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of two negative numbers, $-8$ and $-6.$ So the product will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-8)\\cdot (-6)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $8$ and $6$ without any signs: $8\\cdot 6=48.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-8)\\cdot (-6)=48.\n$$",
