      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$(-2)\\cdot (-24)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of two negative numbers, $-2$ and $-24.$ So the product will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot (-24)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $2$ and $24$ without any signs: $2\\cdot 24=48.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot (-24)=48.\n$$",
