      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$7\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-5)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of a positive and a negative, which gives a negative:\n\n$$\n7\\cdot (-2)=-14\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{7\\cdot (-2)}_{⏟}}_{-14}\\cdot (-5)=(-14)\\cdot (-5).\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that the product of two negatives gives a positive:\n\n$$\n(-14)\\cdot (-5)=14\\cdot 5=70\n$$",
