    "q-2131": {
      "dom_id": "step-q2131",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$(-3)\\cdot 4\\cdot (-2)=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of a negative and a positive, which gives a negative:\n\n$$\n(-3)\\cdot 4=-12\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{(-3)\\cdot 4}_{⏟}}_{-12}\\cdot (-2)=(-12)\\cdot (-2).\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that the product of two negatives gives a positive:\n\n$$\n(-12)\\cdot (-2)=12\\cdot 2=24\n$$",
