      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$(-6)\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 2=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of two negatives, which gives a positive:\n\n$$\n(-6)\\cdot (-4)=24\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{(-6)\\cdot (-4)}_{⏟}}_{24}\\cdot 2=24\\cdot 2.\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that the product of two positives gives a positive:\n\n$$\n24\\cdot 2=48\n$$",
