    "q-180905": {
      "dom_id": "step-q180905",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$(-\\frac{4}{7})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of a negative number and a positive number, so the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{4}{7})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) & =-(\\frac{4}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(\\frac{4}{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}) & =-(\\frac{4\\cdot 1}{7\\cdot 2}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}{7\\cdot 2}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{2}\\cdot 1}{7\\cdot \\cancel{2}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2}{7}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
