      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$(-\\frac{7}{3})\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of a negative number and a positive number, so the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{7}{3})\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=-(\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4})\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}) & =-(\\frac{7\\cdot 5}{3\\cdot 4}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{35}{12}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{35}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
