    "q-43042": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43042",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$(-\\frac{5}{3})\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of two negative numbers, so the product will be positive, and we can drop the minus signs as follows:\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{5}{3})\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{4})=\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{5\\cdot 3}{3\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot \\cancel{3}}{\\cancel{3}\\cdot 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
