    "q-43043": {
      "dom_id": "step-q43043",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{2})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of a positive number and a negative number, so the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{2})=-(\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2})\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}) & =-(\\frac{4\\cdot 9}{3\\cdot 2}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot 3}{3\\cdot 2}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{3}}{\\cancel{3}\\cdot \\cancel{2}}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{6}{1}) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-43043-a",
