    "q-99503": {
      "dom_id": "step-q99503",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$4\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{16})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We have a product of a positive number and a negative number, so the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n4\\cdot (-\\frac{3}{16})=-(4\\cdot \\frac{3}{16})\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(4\\cdot \\frac{3}{16}) & =-(\\frac{4\\cdot 3}{16}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{4\\cdot 3}{4\\cdot 4}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 3}{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 4}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
